+# The Daily Grind account preview
+
+A responsive, dependency-free account interface on the Daily Grind homepage.
+
+## Build
+
+`npm run build` checks JavaScript syntax, duplicate HTML IDs, and SVG references, then copies the static site into `dist/`. No server entrypoint is imported. Serve the static files on HTTPS or localhost when deploying; native passkeys require a secure context and a supported browser/authenticator. No dev or preview server is needed to build.
+
+## Account flows
+
+- The initial Alex Johnson account is an explicitly labeled preview with two example passkeys. Example keys cannot authenticate. Preview-only reauthentication clearly asks to simulate the check.
+- Sign out to access passkey sign-in and registration. Registration creates a real browser passkey and a local account only after enrollment succeeds. Cancellation does not create an account.
+- Add real passkeys through the browser's WebAuthn prompt. Name and rename keys, and remove keys after confirmation and reauthentication. The last enrolled passkey cannot be removed, even if sample keys remain.
+- Profile updates require reauthentication. Duplicate local email addresses and blank names are rejected. Email changes do not claim ownership verification or send email.
+- Passkey sign-in verifies an ES256 signature locally, along with challenge, ceremony type, origin, relying-party hash, user presence, user verification, and user handle where present.
+- Profile records and public keys are stored in localStorage; the selected account is stored in sessionStorage. Private keys and biometrics remain with the authenticator. Storage restrictions are reported, and changes then last for the visit only.
+- Rewards, menu, and orders are preview content. Checkout, support, legal policies, email verification, and actual rewards services are not connected.
+
+## Production boundary
+
+**This is a UI and browser-passkey demonstration, not a production authentication service.** Local storage and local verification are user-controlled and do not secure server resources. Session selection is UI state, not a server-authenticated session. Do not store sensitive information in this preview.
+
+Before using real customer accounts, implement server-issued, single-use, expiring challenges; server-side WebAuthn registration and assertion verification (using an audited library); a durable credential database, signature-counter handling, authenticated authorization for mutations, secure HttpOnly sessions, CSRF protection, rate limiting, verified email changes, and account recovery. Reauthentication authorization must be short-lived and bound to the intended action. Enforce the final-credential rule on the server as well. The preview must not be treated as a fallback that bypasses production authentication.
+
+Public profile email changes update the local profile; authenticators may retain the original credential display email. Removing a key from this UI removes its local association, not the private key in a password manager. Clearing browser storage removes local accounts, but does not remove authenticator credentials.
+
+WebAuthn implementation references: [W3C WebAuthn](https://www.w3.org/TR/webauthn-3/), [MDN getPublicKey](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/AuthenticatorAttestationResponse/getPublicKey), and [MDN authenticator data](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Web_Authentication_API/Authenticator_data).
+
+Google Fonts supplies DM Sans and Manrope. The coffee photograph is hosted by Unsplash. The interface uses inline SVG icons; no generated images are used.
